            <ArticleTitle>Inflammatory fibroid polyp of jejunum causing jejuno-jejunal intussusception.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>190-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intussusceptions originating in the jejunum are rare. We report a 20-year-old woman who had a chronic jejuno-jejunal intussusception due to an inflammatory fibroid polyp manifesting in the post-partum period as peritonitis. Resection-anastomosis of the intussuscepted segment was done. She is well one year later.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
